# Regenerated by the pipeline, too large to track. data/ holds the imported
# molecule table, the series and Monroe's embedding; predictions/ the tidy
# per-fold files of every arm, most of them copies from the source studies;
# work/ the private copies of the release, the per-fold encoders, the SCM parts
# and claims, and the paper splits.
data/
folds/
predictions/
diagnostics/
logs/
work/
scratch/
bin/
# The sweep's raw output. 08_collect_metrics.py reduces it to fold_metrics.csv
# and series_metrics.csv, which are what every figure, table and the report
# read, so those are tracked.
results/*/predictions_all.parquet
# Figures are cheap to rebuild. The ones the report shows are tracked, so a
# checkout without the predictions still shows them.
results/*/figures/*
!results/*/figures/tukey_spearman_series.png
!results/*/figures/tukey_mae.png
!results/*/figures/series_scatter.png

# The report is built here; its builder publishes the copy in docs/reports/.
results/report.html

# Reference material and third-party weights, not ours to redistribute: the
# paper, and the authors' checkpoints and fitted SCMs.
*.pdf
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.pkl
